                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "kMgoV",
                      "name": "Scenario Column Title",
                      "fill": "$blue",
                      "content": "ORDERED REAL-UI SCENARIO",
                      "fontFamily": "$fontBody",
                      "fontSize": 9,
                      "fontWeight": "850"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "IRp3W",
                      "name": "Scenario Test Paths",
                      "fill": "$codeText",
                      "content": "tests/ui_workspace.rs\ntests/cases/httpbingo/responses.json",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$fontMono",
                      "fontSize": 8,
                      "fontWeight": "700"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "K4P3n",
                      "name": "Scenario Ordered Steps",
                      "fill": "$muted",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "1 · Focus the URL input, type https://httpbingo.org/bytes/64, then click Send directly without Enter, Tab, blur, Add, or submit-time backfill.\n2 · Binary response shows application/octet-stream and 64 B received; UTF-8 rendering and text Copy are absent.\n3 · Click Save as… with the injected test destination; saved bytes exactly equal the received ResponsePayload and no second request is sent.\n4 · Send GET /range/128 with Range: bytes=32-63; verify 206 Partial Content, Content-Range: bytes 32-63/128, and 32 B.\n5 · Send GET /stream/5; observe ResponseState::Receiving before ResponseState::Success and a successful History entry.\n6 · Send /drip, cancel while receiving, and verify transport read stops, late chunks are ignored, the spool is removed, and History does not gain success.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$fontBody",
                      "fontSize": 8,
                      "fontWeight": "650"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "p6Kig",
                  "name": "Observable Assertions · Verification Contract",
                  "width": 484,
                  "height": "fill_container",
                  "fill": "$greenSoft",
                  "cornerRadius": 12,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 11,
                  "padding": 18,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "c14xJ",
                      "name": "Assertions Column Title",
                      "fill": "$green",
                      "content": "OBSERVABLE ASSERTIONS · STABLE SUBSET",
                      "fontFamily": "$fontBody",
                      "fontSize": 9,
                      "fontWeight": "850"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "w9eOrD",
                      "name": "Binary and Range Assertions",
                      "fill": "$muted",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "• /bytes/:n values are not asserted; byte_len, Content-Type, and disk bytes are exact.\n• /range/:n asserts 206 + Content-Range + the exact received 32-byte slice.\n• Binary payload is never decoded into String and exposes Save as… instead of text Copy.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$fontBody",
                      "fontSize": 8,
                      "fontWeight": "650"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "clY6u",
                      "name": "Streaming Lifecycle Assertions",
                      "fill": "$muted",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "• Receiving reports chunks / bytes and uses an indeterminate bar when total length is unknown.\n• Streaming text preview ≤ 64 KiB; full binary / streamed payload is file-backed from the first chunk.\n• Cancel commits ResponseState::Cancelled; stale request_id chunks cannot overwrite it; no success History row.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$fontBody",
                      "fontSize": 8,
                      "fontWeight": "650"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "ykE15",
                      "name": "Atomic Save Assertions",
                      "fill": "$muted",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "• copy canonical spool → <destination>.part → fsync → atomic rename.\n• A save or cleanup failure never exposes a partial file under the requested final filename.\n• Normal failure removes .part; cleanup failure retains the .part suffix and exposes Reveal / Delete.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$fontBody",
                      "fontSize": 8,
                      "fontWeight": "650"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "CTDy5",
                  "name": "Scope and Non-Goals",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": "fill_container",
                  "fill": "$accentSoft",
                  "cornerRadius": 12,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 11,
                  "padding": 18,
                  "children": [
